{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And he went up to meet Israel.</b> This means: he had an elevation, for having gone to meet his father to honor him. Another explanation: it says ויעל because the land of Goshen is higher than the land of Egypt, for it stands at the border of the land of Israel, as it is said: ״גשן וחולון וגילה״. And because Judah went on his father's behalf to Joseph to direct him to Goshen, he merited and it fell to his portion. And Pharaoh gave Goshen to Sarah our mother, and therefore Israel chose it and it fell to their portion, and Egypt did not contest it."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:10.000710890Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}